 :problem
 {:source "user direction 2026-07-07: continuing the pivot to big decisions needing user
           input, chose 'crypto/chain + wallet selection' as the next area, then (after
           research surfaced that the chain stack is already decided at the etzhayyim level)
           chose 'ADR only' as this round's scope -- no code changes"
  :prior_state
  {:what "babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability HARD-holds every subscribe/tip/ppv
          proposal (ADR-2607062200, honest-default) -- no payment rail has ever been designed
          or implemented for net-babiniku"}
  :research_findings
  {:chain_stack_already_decided
   {:source "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605172100 (status: proposed)"
    :stack "Base L2, USDC (EURC/JPYC also whitelisted per kawase-yui), ERC-4337 smart accounts
            via Coinbase Smart Wallet with WebAuthn passkey signing (payer's own device holds
            custody, no seed phrase/extension), Superfluid (streaming subs), 0xSplits (revenue
            splits), Gnosis Safe (escrow), an etzhayyim-operated Paymaster. Custom token
            explicitly rejected. Fiat processors prohibited in etzhayyim substrate. junbi
            (ADR-2607021800) already holds USDC/EURC/JPYC in a Base L2 Safe under Shamir-split
            custody keys as the reserve-treasury precedent."
    :conclusion "there is no chain to pick for net-babiniku -- consuming this existing rail is
                the only option consistent with ADR-2605211950's substrate boundary"}
   :substrate_boundary
   {:source "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605211950 (status: active)"
    :rule "decentralized primitives (Ethereum/Base L2/ERC-4337/did:web/did:plc/etc.) are
          etzhayyim-EXCLUSIVE; centralized substrate (fiat/Datomic/operator storage/JWT) is
          vendor-EXCLUSIVE. net-babiniku is a vendor app (Cloudflare Pages, no chain code) --
          must never hold a private key or scaffold settlement logic itself"
    :worked_crossover_direction "only etzhayyim-calls-vendor (a vendor-hosted paid-tier fiat
                                XRPC an etzhayyim app calls as progressive enhancement) is
                                worked out. The OPPOSITE direction -- vendor calling into
                                etzhayyim for crypto settlement, which is what net-babiniku
                                needs -- has NO worked example yet"}
   :consent_capability_precedent
   {:source "orgs/etzhayyim/root/20-actors/karute/actor-manifest.jsonld +
             90-docs/adr/2605231401 (karute<->iryo billing bridge)"
    :shape "com.etzhayyim.consent.capability: {version, granterDid, granteeDid, purpose, scope,
            resourceUris?, issuedAt, expiresAt, constraints{maxQueriesPerDay?, redactionLevel?,
            downstreamRedistribution?, auditWebhookDid?}, delegationPath?, revokedAt?/
            revokedBy?/revocationReason?, signature{alg, value, keyId}} -- Ed25519-signed,
            publicly verifiable delegation record"
    :fit "a useful TEMPLATE (signed/scoped/expiring/revocable delegation), not a drop-in fit --
         shaped for health-data ACCESS CONSENT (query scope, redaction level), not payment
         AUTHORIZATION. Also both karute and iryo are etzhayyim/root actors -- an intra-
         substrate handoff, not a worked vendor<->etzhayyim example."
    :honesty_note "signConsentCapability -- the actual signing call -- is NOT implemented
                  anywhere; the ADR itself calls it 'currently a stub in the actor manifest'"}
   :sdk_implementation_state
   {:source "orgs/etzhayyim/root/20-actors/etzhayyim-sdk/src/{index.ts,pay.ts}"
    :real "pay() -- a one-off EOA USDC transfer + AT record, returns
          PaymentReceipt{txHash, blockNumber, recordUri, ...}. THE ONLY REAL PRIMITIVE."
    :stubs "payStream (Superfluid CFAv1.createFlow, TODO), payStreamStop, escrowOpen (Gnosis
           Safe 2-of-3 deploy, TODO), escrowRelease, splitDistribute (0xSplits
           distributeERC20, TODO), verify (5-step MST/anchor/Merkle-proof TODO, would return
           VerifyResult{included, anchoredAt?, merklePath?, reason?}) -- ALL THROW TODAY"
    :relevance_to_net_babiniku "subscriptions need payStream (stub); the 80/20 creator split
                               (ADR-2607062200) needs splitDistribute (stub); confirming ANY
                               payment before granting an entitlement needs verify() (stub) --
                               so even :tip, whose settlement primitive (pay()) is real, has
                               no safe path to unlock an entitlement without verify()"}}}

 :decision
 {:no_new_chain_or_wallet
  {:what "net-babiniku consumes etzhayyim's existing rail exactly as decided -- Base L2, USDC/
          EURC/JPYC, ERC-4337 Coinbase Smart Wallet + passkey signing, via @etzhayyim/sdk.
          Never imports viem, holds a key, or calls a chain RPC directly"}
  :signing_stays_client_side
  {:what "the payer's Coinbase Smart Wallet is passkey-based (WebAuthn) -- the payment
          UserOperation must be signed in the viewer's browser, never on net-babiniku's
          Cloudflare Pages Function server"
   :why "matches orgs/etzhayyim/root/CLAUDE.md's substrate boundary table: 'Any platform-held
        private key ... in etzhayyim-operated Workers/pods/CronJobs' is Prohibited -- the same
        invariant applies to a vendor server proxying signing material"
   :contrast_with_chat_backend "opposite role from ADR-2607070800's LLM chat call: there, the
                                secret (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) must stay server-side and never
                                reach the browser; here, the signing capability must stay in
                                the payer's browser/device and never be proxied through
                                net-babiniku's server. The server's only role is to receive and
                                verify a settlement receipt before honoring an entitlement."}
  :new_lexicon
  {:what "net.babiniku.monetization.capability -- proposed, follows karute's signed/scoped/
          expiring/revocable pattern but with payment-shaped fields, NOT a reuse of
          com.etzhayyim.consent.capability"
   :shape {:version 1
           :payerDid "DID -- viewer's did:key from their Smart Wallet"
           :payeeDid "DID -- creator's (or platform's, for tips) did"
           :purpose "\"subscribe\" | \"tip\" | \"ppv\""
           :scope "{characterId, tier?, sceneId?} -- mirrors babiniku.monetization's existing
                   proposal shape"
           :amount "{asset: \"USDC\"|\"EURC\"|\"JPYC\", value: string} -- string, not float,
                    matching PaymentReceipt's bigint-safe pattern"
           :recurrence "{intervalDays: int}, present only for :subscribe (drives payStream)"
           :issuedAt "ISO-8601" :expiresAt "ISO-8601"
           :constraints "{maxTotalValue?: string, revocable: bool}"
           :signature "{alg: \"ed25519\", value: base64, keyId: DID-verification-method}"}
   :mirrors_existing_proposal_shape "1:1 with babiniku.monetization's {:kind :subscribe/:tip/
                                     :ppv, :character-id, ...} -- review-proposal's existing
                                     HARD-hold logic doesn't need to change shape when a real
                                     capability eventually replaces unprovisioned-capability"}
  :new_crossover_pattern_proposed_not_ratified
  {:what "vendor calls @etzhayyim/sdk client-side for payer-signed settlement, then sends only
          the resulting {txHash, recordUri} receipt to its own server for Etzhayyim.verify()
          before honoring an entitlement -- no consent-capability record needs to reach
          net-babiniku's own Datomic-shaped storage beyond the receipt + verification result"
   :status "PROPOSED, not ratified -- ADR-2605211950 only worked out the opposite direction.
           This ADR's own Status field reflects that: net-babiniku is not the right place to
           unilaterally decide an etzhayyim-wide crossover pattern; whoever owns
           ADR-2605211950/2605172100 should review this before implementation"}
  :capability_stays_unprovisioned
  {:what "babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability remains the only implementation for
          ALL THREE proposal kinds -- this ADR's design does not change the HARD-hold status
          quo"
   :why "payStream (needed for :subscribe), splitDistribute (needed for the 80/20 split), and
        verify (needed to confirm ANY settlement before granting ANY entitlement) are all
        unimplemented stubs in @etzhayyim/sdk today. Even :tip, whose settlement primitive
        (pay()) is real, has no safe unlock path without verify()."
   :purpose_of_this_adr "so that when etzhayyim's own primitives mature, net-babiniku has a
                         concrete, reviewed integration plan to switch on rather than a
                         redesign-from-scratch"}}

 :consequences
 {:no_code_changes "by explicit user direction, this ADR ships with zero code changes --
                    babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability is unchanged; every
                    subscribe/tip/PPV proposal continues to HARD-hold"
  :blocked_on_etzhayyim_side "payStream/splitDistribute/verify need to move from stub to
                             implementation in @etzhayyim/sdk before any of this can be built,
                             regardless of anything net-babiniku does"
  :needs_etzhayyim_side_review "the vendor->etzhayyim crossover pattern (decision #4) needs
                               review from whoever maintains ADR-2605211950/2605172100 before
                               net-babiniku (or any other vendor app) implements against it"
  :lexicon_unimplemented "net.babiniku.monetization.capability is a proposed lexicon,
                         unimplemented anywhere -- if accepted, needs a signing implementation
                         (client-side, inside whatever wallet-connection UI wraps
                         @etzhayyim/sdk's payer flow), not built by this ADR either"
  :followup "once etzhayyim's primitives exist, verify this ADR's proposed field shapes against
            whatever @etzhayyim/sdk actually ships -- this is a proposal, not a contract
            etzhayyim has agreed to"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "pick our own chain/wallet stack for net-babiniku, independent of etzhayyim"
   :rejected_because "directly violates ADR-2605211950's substrate-axis rule (decentralized
                      primitives are etzhayyim-exclusive); would also duplicate real
                      engineering (Base L2 integration, Paymaster, custody) etzhayyim has
                      already built"}
  {:option "proxy the payer's signing through net-babiniku's Cloudflare Function"
   :rejected_because "would require the server to hold or relay signing material for the
                      payer's passkey-based Smart Wallet, violating the explicit 'no
                      platform-held private key' prohibition in etzhayyim/root's CLAUDE.md
                      substrate boundary table. Signing must stay client-side."}
  {:option "reuse com.etzhayyim.consent.capability as-is instead of a new lexicon"
   :rejected_because "its fields (query scope, redaction level, audit webhook) are shaped for
                      health-data access consent, not value-transfer authorization; forcing
                      payment semantics into that shape is a worse fit than a small new
                      lexicon following the same signed/scoped/expiring/revocable pattern"}
  {:option "treat pay()'s one working code path as enough to unlock :tip now"
   :rejected_because "without verify(), net-babiniku would have no way to confirm a claimed
                      payment actually settled on-chain before granting an entitlement -- worse
                      than the current honest HARD-hold, not better"}
  {:option "silently assume the vendor->etzhayyim crossover direction is already covered by
            ADR-2605211950's existing crossover clause"
   :rejected_because "that clause is directionally etzhayyim-calls-vendor (fiat progressive
                      enhancement); assuming it also covers vendor-calls-etzhayyim (crypto
                      settlement) would be inventing an architectural decision this ADR isn't
                      authorized to make unilaterally -- surfaced explicitly instead (decision
                      #4, consequences)"}]}